<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cenbank sells dollar-indexed notes.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cenbank sells dollar-indexed notes.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank sold Monday a total face value of 300 million reais in dollar-indexed special series of Central Bank Notes (NBC-E), dealers said.</p>
<p>The notes, which have a six-month maturity and expire on Sept 11, 1997, will pay an annual yield of 11.39 percent plus the variation of the foreign exchange rate in the period, they added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248 5418))</p>
